Put cuML's CPU cluster labels on the points' device.

Upstream pin: shape-of-motion @ 579753e1c7ba96f60cd7690e5b835627bd1935e9

Shape of Motion targets torch 2.1. torch >= 2.11, which we need for sm_120, is stricter about
indexing a CUDA tensor with a CPU index. cuML returns cluster labels on CPU while the points and
centers are on CUDA, so motion-basis init raises. Both edits are needed: the per-cluster centre
reduction AND the labels returned to the caller.

Without it: motion-basis initialisation fails on every run.
diff --git a/flow3d/init_utils.py b/flow3d/init_utils.py
index 9790b36..db72848 100644
--- a/flow3d/init_utils.py
+++ b/flow3d/init_utils.py
@@ -581,12 +581,12 @@ def sample_initial_bases_centers(
     num_bases = labels.max().item() + 1
     sampled_centers = torch.stack(
         [
-            means_canonical[torch.tensor(labels == i)].median(dim=0).values
+            means_canonical[torch.tensor(labels == i, device=means_canonical.device)].median(dim=0).values
             for i in range(num_bases)
         ]
     )[None]
     print("number of {} clusters: ".format(mode), num_bases)
-    return sampled_centers, num_bases, torch.tensor(labels)
+    return sampled_centers, num_bases, torch.tensor(labels, device=means_canonical.device)
 
 
